---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { langFromUrl } from '../lib/registry';

const lang = langFromUrl(Astro.url);
---
<Layout lang={lang} title="Methodology & Epistemic Rules" activeNav="methodology">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="border-b border-hoba-border pb-6">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase font-bold text-hoba-accent tracking-wider">Epistemic Foundation</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black font-mono text-hoba-text mt-1">HOBA Methodology</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-hoba-muted mt-2">
        How hoba decomposes hiring uncertainty, enforces explicit evidence levels, and prevents false certainty.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Principle -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-hoba-border bg-hoba-card/60">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-hoba-text mb-2">Core Design Rule</h2>
      <blockquote class="text-sm font-mono text-hoba-accent border-l-2 border-hoba-accent pl-4 my-3 italic">
        "hoba must make uncertainty more explicit, not merely replace one unsupported story with another."
      </blockquote>
      <p class="text-xs text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">
        An observation is not a cause. A rejection message is not necessarily a reason. A compatible mechanism is not a proven mechanism.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The 4 Epistemic Verbs -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-hoba-border bg-hoba-card space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-hoba-text">The Four Epistemic Verbs</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-hoba-muted">All claims in HOBA must strictly use one of four calibrated verbs:</p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs font-mono">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-hoba-bg border border-hoba-border">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-bold block mb-1">1. Observed</span>
          <p class="text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">Directly present in empirical evidence or submission logs (e.g. rejection email timestamp, job post URL).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-hoba-bg border border-hoba-border">
          <span class="text-blue-400 font-bold block mb-1">2. Compatible with</span>
          <p class="text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">The mechanism could logically produce the observation given the structural gate. No probability implied.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-hoba-bg border border-hoba-border">
          <span class="text-amber-400 font-bold block mb-1">3. Supported</span>
          <p class="text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">Empirical research or secondary signals raise confidence beyond mere logical compatibility.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-hoba-bg border border-hoba-border">
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold block mb-1">4. Established</span>
          <p class="text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">Direct verification supports the precise causal claim rendered (e.g. verified ATS parsing regex).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Preserving Honest Baselines -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-hoba-border bg-hoba-card/60 space-y-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-hoba-text">Preservation of Honest Baselines</h2>
      <p class="text-hoba-muted">
        A credible registry cannot become an echo chamber that blames external factors for every outcome. Genuine skill-depth shortfalls, communication friction, and leveling mismatches are first-class, mandatory baseline mechanisms in the ontology (<code class="text-emerald-300">honest_baseline: true</code>).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Evidence Model (anchor target for evidence record URLs) -->
    <div id="evidence" class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-hoba-border bg-hoba-card space-y-4 text-xs">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-hoba-text">Evidence Records & Levels</h2>
      <p class="text-hoba-muted leading-relaxed">
        Every node declares an <code class="text-hoba-accent">evidence_level</code> and may cite <code class="text-hoba-accent">EVD-xxx</code> records.
        Evidence <em>kinds</em> describe the source (primary, research, reporting, survey, anecdote, illustrative);
        evidence <em>levels</em> describe how far the claim is supported (established, supported, hypothesis, illustrative).
        A citation raises a claim to "supported" only when it addresses the specific mechanism, not the general topic.
      </p>
      <p class="text-amber-300/90 leading-relaxed">
        The current evidence catalog is a development scaffold: records describe the class of source the maintainers intend to cite
        and do not yet point at external publications. Treat "established" and "supported" levels as provisional until each record links a primary source.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Non-Goals -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-rose-900/40 bg-rose-950/20 space-y-3 text-xs">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold font-mono text-rose-300">Explicit Non-Goals</h2>
      <p class="text-rose-200/80">hoba is explicitly NOT:</p>
      <ul class="space-y-1 text-rose-200/80 list-disc list-inside">
        <li>A company or recruiter blacklist;</li>
        <li>A "ghost job" accusation engine;</li>
        <li>A personal rejection diary or doom tracker;</li>
        <li>A coaching service promising employment outcomes;</li>
        <li>A legal discrimination determination tool.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
